<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">4 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 4 January, from 46 BCE to 1959.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">46 BCE <span class="tih-ago">1,980 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Caesar narrowly escapes defeat at the Battle of Ruspina</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In North Africa, Julius Caesar's outnumbered army was surrounded by Republican forces under Titus Labienus. Caesar fought his way back to camp, surviving to defeat his enemies at Thapsus three months later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1878 CE <span class="tih-ago">148 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Russian troops take Sofia from the Ottomans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the Russo-Turkish War, Russian forces under General Gurko entered Sofia, ending nearly five centuries of Ottoman rule. The city became the capital of the new Bulgarian state the following year.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1884 CE <span class="tih-ago">142 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fabian Society founded in London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A group of middle-class reformers founded the Fabian Society to promote socialism through gradual reform rather than revolution. Members such as the Webbs and George Bernard Shaw later helped shape the Labour Party.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1918 CE <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet Russia recognises Finland's independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lenin's government confirmed Finnish independence, declared in December 1917. Sweden, Germany and France recognised the new state the same day, though Finland soon slid into civil war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1948 CE <span class="tih-ago">78 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Burma becomes independent from Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Burma left British rule as an independent republic outside the Commonwealth, at an hour chosen by astrologers. Independence hero Aung San had been assassinated six months earlier, and civil conflict soon followed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-nations.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1951 CE <span class="tih-ago">75 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Chinese and North Korean forces capture Seoul</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">United Nations troops abandoned Seoul as Chinese and North Korean armies advanced, the third time the city had changed hands in the Korean War. UN forces retook it in March.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1958 CE <span class="tih-ago">68 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sputnik 1 falls from orbit</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The first artificial satellite burned up in the atmosphere after three months and some 1,400 orbits. Its launch the previous October had shocked the United States and started the space race.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1959 CE <span class="tih-ago">67 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Luna 1 becomes the first spacecraft to pass the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Soviet probe flew within about 6,000 km of the Moon's surface before heading into orbit around the Sun. Its instruments made the first direct measurements of the solar wind.</p></div></li></ol>
